&HEAD CHID='day6_broken', TITLE='Day 6 exercise: this case runs, and it is wrong in three places' /

 PyroSim 7-day guide - DAY 6 EXERCISE. FDS finishes this case with one
 warning and no error, yet three things are wrong. Find them from the .out file,
 the CSV files and Smokeview before you look at the answer in the guide.
 PyroSim writes a file like this one; FDS reads it. Everything between a '&'
 and the next '/' is an instruction. Text outside those pairs, like this, is
 ignored, which is why it can hold comments.

 GEOMETRY. Two meshes of 10 cm cubes. ROOM is the ISO 9705 room itself; its
 boundaries act as the back wall, side walls, floor and ceiling. OUTSIDE is the
 space beyond the door, 2.4 m deep and 3 m tall, so the smoke leaving the door
 has room to rise before it reaches an open boundary. The front wall is an
 obstruction with the door cut through it. Run with one MPI process per mesh.

&MESH ID='ROOM',    IJK=36,24,24, XB=0.0,3.6,  0.0,2.4, 0.0,2.4 /
&MESH ID='OUTSIDE', IJK=24,36,30, XB=3.6,6.0, -0.6,3.0, 0.0,3.0 /

&TIME T_END=1200.0 /
&DUMP DT_DEVC=1.0, DT_HRR=1.0, DT_SLCF=5.0 /

 FIRE CHEMISTRY. Propane, with soot and CO yields for a well-ventilated flame.

&REAC FUEL='PROPANE', SOOT_YIELD=0.024, CO_YIELD=0.005 /

 LINING. Every wall, floor and ceiling that is not given another surface.
 ISO 9705-1:2016 asks only for a non-combustible material of 600 +/- 200 kg/m3,
 at least 20 mm thick. The properties below are aerated concrete from NUREG-1805
 Table 2-3 (Klote and Milke 2002); 100 mm matches BRANZ's lightweight panels.

&MATL ID='AERATED CONCRETE', CONDUCTIVITY=0.26, SPECIFIC_HEAT=0.96, DENSITY=500.0 /
&SURF ID='ROOM LINING', MATL_ID='AERATED CONCRETE', THICKNESS=0.1, COLOR='GRAY 80', DEFAULT=.TRUE. /

&OBST ID='Front wall', XB=3.6,3.7, 0.0,2.4, 0.0,2.4, SURF_ID='ROOM LINING' /
&HOLE ID='Door', XB=3.40,3.50, 0.8,1.6, 0.0,2.0 /

 OUTSIDE. Open boundaries on the far, side and top faces of the OUTSIDE mesh let
 smoke leave and fresh air come in. The floor and the building face stay solid.

&VENT ID='Open +x',  XB=6.0,6.0, -0.6,3.0, 0.0,3.0, SURF_ID='OPEN' /
&VENT ID='Open -y',  XB=3.6,6.0, -0.6,-0.6, 0.0,3.0, SURF_ID='OPEN' /
&VENT ID='Open +y',  XB=3.6,6.0,  3.0,3.0, 0.0,3.0, SURF_ID='OPEN' /
&VENT ID='Open top', XB=3.6,6.0, -0.6,3.0, 3.0,3.0, SURF_ID='OPEN' /

 BURNER. ISO 9705-1:2016 uses a 0.17 x 0.17 m propane sand burner in the corner
 opposite the door, top 146 mm above the floor. On 10 cm cells it is drawn as
 0.2 x 0.2 m with its top at 0.1 m, the nearest cell faces.
 The ramp rises to one third of full output over 10 s, holds for 590 s, rises
 to full over 10 s, and holds for the last 590 s.

&SURF ID='BURNER', HRRPUA=300.0, RAMP_Q='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', COLOR='RED' /
&RAMP ID='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', T=0.0,    F=0.0 /
&RAMP ID='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', T=10.0,   F=0.3333 /
&RAMP ID='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', T=600.0,  F=0.3333 /
&RAMP ID='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', T=610.0,  F=1.0 /
&RAMP ID='ISO 9705 PROGRAMME', T=1200.0, F=1.0 /
&OBST ID='Burner', XB=0.0,0.2, 0.0,0.2, 0.0,0.1, SURF_IDS='BURNER','ROOM LINING','ROOM LINING' /

 EDUCATIONAL SENSOR POSITIONS. Each carries TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE'. Without
 it FDS reports a device as a TIME AVERAGE over the output interval, and the
 educational exporter takes its 5 s frames by decimation precisely so that nothing is
 averaged. FED is left alone: that quantity is a running time integral by
 definition. Check it in any run: search the .out file for TEMPORAL STATISTIC.
 S1 at the room centre, S2 near the door. Thermocouple,
 CO and smoke at the ceiling, where a detector would be; visibility, gases and
 FED at head height.

&DEVC ID='S1_T',   QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,2.35 /
&DEVC ID='S1_CO',  QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='CARBON MONOXIDE', CONVERSION_FACTOR=1.0E6, UNITS='ppm', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,2.35 /
&DEVC ID='S1_OD',  QUANTITY='OPTICAL DENSITY', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,2.35 /
&DEVC ID='S1_VIS', QUANTITY='VISIBILITY', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S1_FED', QUANTITY='FED', XYZ=1.85,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S1_O2',  QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='OXYGEN', CONVERSION_FACTOR=100.0, UNITS='%', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S1_CO2', QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='CARBON DIOXIDE', CONVERSION_FACTOR=100.0, UNITS='%', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=1.85,1.25,1.85 /

&DEVC ID='S2_T',   QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,2.45 /
&DEVC ID='S2_CO',  QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='CARBON MONOXIDE', CONVERSION_FACTOR=1.0E6, UNITS='ppm', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,2.35 /
&DEVC ID='S2_OD',  QUANTITY='OPTICAL DENSITY', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,2.35 /
&DEVC ID='S2_VIS', QUANTITY='VISIBILITY', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S2_FED', QUANTITY='FED', XYZ=3.25,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S2_O2',  QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='OXYGEN', CONVERSION_FACTOR=100.0, UNITS='%', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='S2_CO2', QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='CARBON DIOXIDE', CONVERSION_FACTOR=100.0, UNITS='%', TEMPORAL_STATISTIC='INSTANT VALUE', XYZ=3.25,1.25,1.85 /

 THERMOCOUPLE TREE in the front corner, and one in the doorway.

&DEVC ID='TC_025', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,0.25 /
&DEVC ID='TC_065', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,0.65 /
&DEVC ID='TC_105', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,1.05 /
&DEVC ID='TC_145', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,1.45 /
&DEVC ID='TC_185', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,1.85 /
&DEVC ID='TC_225', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,2.25 /
&DEVC ID='TC_235', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.25,2.15,2.35 /

&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_015', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,0.15 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_055', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,0.55 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_095', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,0.95 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_135', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,1.35 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_175', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,1.75 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_TC_195', QUANTITY='THERMOCOUPLE', XYZ=3.65,1.25,1.95 /

 SMOKE LAYER, estimated along a vertical line through the corner tree.

&DEVC ID='LAYER_H', QUANTITY='LAYER HEIGHT',      XB=3.25,3.25, 2.15,2.15, 0.0,2.4 /
&DEVC ID='UPPER_T', QUANTITY='UPPER TEMPERATURE', XB=3.25,3.25, 2.15,2.15, 0.0,2.4 /
&DEVC ID='LOWER_T', QUANTITY='LOWER TEMPERATURE', XB=3.25,3.25, 2.15,2.15, 0.0,2.4 /

 FLASHOVER INDICATOR: heat flux reaching the floor at the room centre.

&DEVC ID='FLOOR_FLUX', QUANTITY='GAUGE HEAT FLUX', XYZ=1.85,1.25,0.0, IOR=3 /

 DOORWAY FLOWS: hot gas out through the top, fresh air in at the bottom.

&DEVC ID='DOOR_OUT', QUANTITY='MASS FLUX X', SPATIAL_STATISTIC='AREA INTEGRAL', QUANTITY_RANGE(1)=0.0, XB=3.65,3.65, 0.8,1.6, 0.0,2.0 /
&DEVC ID='DOOR_IN',  QUANTITY='MASS FLUX X', SPATIAL_STATISTIC='AREA INTEGRAL', QUANTITY_RANGE(2)=0.0, XB=3.65,3.65, 0.8,1.6, 0.0,2.0 /

 SLICES for pictures in Smokeview or PyroSim Results.

&SLCF PBY=1.25, QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE', VECTOR=.TRUE. /
&SLCF PBY=1.25, QUANTITY='VOLUME FRACTION', SPEC_ID='CARBON MONOXIDE' /
&SLCF PBZ=1.85, QUANTITY='VISIBILITY' /
&SLCF PBX=3.65, QUANTITY='TEMPERATURE' /

&TAIL /
